      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While there isn't a universal consensus, a significant and growing body of critical thought strongly challenges the notion of the \"universal museum.\" Critics argue that classifying objects as belonging to one culture while displaying them elsewhere inherently prioritizes Western academic frameworks over originating community narratives. Many contemporary curators are actively moving away from this model toward decolonization, emphasizing collaboration and shared stewardship rather than purely centralized possession.",
      "source": "target",
