      "content": "okay, so it sounds like the tide is really turning. if most contemporary curators are moving toward decolonization and shared stewardship, does that mean the old \"universal museum\" argument is basically just a way to defend holding onto stolen goods? like, is there even a valid scholarly argument left for keeping things, or is that stance just outdated?",
